00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.000
SPEAKER: You've made it to
the last lab in the quest.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.220
After you complete
this lab on Qwiklabs

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.590
you will finally
unlock your badge.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.900
Are you familiar
with Qwiklab quests?

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.090
Quests are a series
of labs organized

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:20.550
by technologies, specific
services, or particular use

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.590
cases.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.900
There's no need to
complete an entire quest

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.440
in a single sitting.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:28.250
But by completing each
individual lab in a quest,

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:32.326
you can earn badges that reflect
your newly acquired skills.

00:00:32.326 --> 00:00:33.950
On this episode,
we're going to go over

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.910
what you'll learn in this final
lab in the GCP Essentials quest

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.420
and set up network and
HTTP load balancers.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.070
In this hands-on on
lab, you'll learn

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.960
the differences
between a network load

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.440
balancer and an
HTTP load balancer

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.990
and how to set them up for
your applications running

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:54.274
on Google Compute
Engine virtual machines.

00:00:54.274 --> 00:00:55.940
This lab will take
you through the steps

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.070
to set up two types
of load balancers

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.960
in Google Cloud Platform--

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:06.170
L3 network load balancer,
L7 HTTPS load balancer.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:08.690
You will create an instance
template with a specified

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:11.120
startup script,
create a target pool

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:12.980
to allow us a
single access point

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:16.490
to all instances in a group,
create a managed instance

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:19.790
group using the instance
template with two VMs,

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.730
view the created instances,
and configure a firewall

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:25.310
to connect to the
machines on port 80,

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.610
create a level 3 network load
balancer targeting the instance

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:32.090
group we created, list the
forwarding rules in our project

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.910
to see the target of our
group is our instance group,

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:37.730
and use the IP address
at the load balancer

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.720
to visit the load
balancer from a browser.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:42.770
In the remainder of
the lab, you will also

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:45.800
create a HTTPS load balancer.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:46.670
Is this it?

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.980
Is this the last
lab on your quest?

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.020
Congratulations-- we
want to hear from you.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.752
Tell us about your experience
following this Qwiklabs quest

00:01:54.752 --> 00:01:56.210
and how you're
applying what you've

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:59.730
learned in your own applications
in the comments below.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.390
See you next month, when we'll
embark on our next quest--

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:03.620
baseline infrastructure.

